  "language": "FROG",
  "title": "Queue : capacité, Preview, perte contrôlée et Flush",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "Queue : capacité, Preview, perte contrôlée et Flush",
    "name_source": "document",
    "description": "Une Queue<f64> de capacité 2 reçoit 10 puis 20. Preview lit 10 sans l'enlever : Status retourne toujours [10,20] et count=2. Lossy Enqueue de 30 évince exactement 10 ; Flush retourne [20,30]. Dequeue avec timeout=0 constate ensuite une file vide, sans créer de valeur. Release ferme le handle et retourne un tableau restant vide.\n\nQueue : capacité, Preview, perte contrôlée et Flush\n\nMode: execution. Profile: studio-draft. Capability: windows-x64/structured-program.\nExpected:\npreview (f64) = 10\ncount (i32) = 2\ncapacity (i32) = 2\nbefore (array<f64>) = [10,20]\noverflow (bool) = true\nevicted (f64) = 10\nflushed (array<f64>) = [20,30]\nempty_timeout (bool) = true\nremaining (array<f64>) = []\nerror_status (bool) = false\nerror_code (i32) = 0\n",
    "author": "",
    "automatic_versioning": false,
    "program_version": "0.0.0.0",
    "tags": ["native", "typed", "resources", "example"],
    "documentation_uri": ""
  },
